#!/bin/sh
# Manual acceptance procedure for issue #1112 (D9): Tailscale as an opt-in
# overlay next to NetBird.
#
# One unprivileged run on a Linux host with KVM proves, with real binaries:
#
#   vms      two qemu VMs on a closed lab link, a Headscale control server and a
#            kernel-TUN tailscaled on each; D4 (CLI, attach and SDK control path)
#            in both directions, plus the recorded D5/D7 observations
#   netbird  the absent-overlays.toml default (NetBird) with a throwaway daemon,
#            without touching the owner's daemon or NetBird
#   macos    zajcaair, no root: the D6 trusted-CLI lookup without a tailscaled and
#            the userspace-networking fail-closed path (needs the vms leg for
#            Headscale)
#
# Every command is recorded as a step directory in the state directory and is
# interpreted only by overlay_evidence.py, which writes the evidence document
# (docs/acceptance/1112-tailscale-overlay.json). Nothing here is judged by this
# script; a failed precondition is recorded as an inconclusive code instead.
# See docs/acceptance/README.md for the procedure, prerequisites, resource budget
# and the exposure statement.
#
# Secrets: pre-auth keys travel only through pipes between the two VMs. They are
# never written on the host, printed, or echoed; no `set -x`.

set -eu

